<section class="before-label article-wide not-prose" aria-labelledby="before-label-heading">
  <header>
    <p>Working chronology</p>
    <h2 id="before-label-heading">Before the label</h2>
  </header>
  <ol>
    <li><time>Late 1950s</time><span>Hugh Romney works the Gaslight basement, where poetry, comedy, jazz, and folk share a room.</span></li>
    <li><time>1961</time><span>Bob Dylan records an informal set at Bonnie Beecher's Minneapolis home.</span></li>
    <li><time>1964</time><span>Beecher performs “Come Wander with Me” for <em>The Twilight Zone</em>.</span></li>
    <li><time>1965</time><span>Bill Graham organizes a Mime Troupe benefit. Hugh and Bonnie meet in Los Angeles.</span></li>
    <li><time>1966–67</time><span>Ballrooms, Acid Tests, light shows, benefits, and communal groups begin to look connected.</span></li>
    <li><time>1968</time><span>The Hog Farm takes its working method on the road.</span></li>
    <li><time>1969</time><span>Woodstock becomes a public demonstration of skills developed elsewhere.</span></li>
  </ol>
  <p class="before-label__note">The dates mark separate working histories. They are not a claim that one person or event caused the next.</p>
</section>

